## sekvent

This project is built on [sekvent]({{sekvent_git_url}}), a Rust backend
framework. The section between the `sekvent:begin` / `sekvent:end` markers is
managed by `cargo sekvent agents`; edit outside it.

### Where things run

- Everything that compiles (check, clippy, tests, coverage) runs on the
  remote builder: `cargo sekvent <command>` forwards to rrb, which syncs the
  tree and runs the command in a container with Docker access for the test
  harness. See the `build-on-rtx` skill.
- `cargo fmt` (the writing form) and in-tree code generation run locally.
- There is no local fallback. If the builder is unreachable, stop and report;
  do not "just run cargo test here". CI runs the same commands locally
  (`CI=true`).

### Commands

```sh
cargo fmt --all                 # local, writes
cargo sekvent check             # remote: cargo check, all targets
cargo sekvent clippy            # remote: clippy -D warnings
cargo sekvent test              # remote: the test suite
cargo sekvent gate              # remote: fmt --check + clippy + tests + boundaries
cargo sekvent coverage          # remote: llvm-cov, per-package line floors
cargo sekvent harness-clean     # remove leftover test containers
```

The gate and the coverage floors (`[coverage]` in `sekvent.toml`, 95 % lines
per package by default) must pass before work is done.

### Configuration

- Each crate reads one `Config` struct with `#[derive(EnvConfig)]`; `main`
  calls `sekvent::config::from_env()`. Tests build it from a `MapSource`,
  never by mutating the process environment.
- Keys under `SEKVENT_` are reserved for the framework (logging, links, the
  harness). Do not invent new ones.
- Secrets are `Secret` fields. Never log, format, `Debug`-print or return a
  secret, token, password, database URL or upstream body; use
  `sekvent::telemetry::truncate_for_log` for untrusted text.
- Fail closed: a missing key is a startup error naming the key, never a
  silent default for anything security-relevant.

### Errors

- Handlers return `AppError`: an `ErrorCode`, a caller-safe message, and
  optionally a reason, metadata and field violations. Internal detail goes in
  the source (`AppError::internal(err)` / `.with_source(err)`), which is
  logged but never sent to the caller.
- Map at the edge only: `AppError` converts to `tonic::Status` and to an
  axum response; do not hand-roll status mapping.

### Tests

- Unit tests next to the code, integration tests in `tests/`.
- No fixed sleeps. Wait on completion signals (channels, join handles,
  `RuntimeHandle::wait`), use `tokio::time::pause` / `start_paused` for
  timers, inject `Clock` where behaviour depends on wall time, and use
  `sekvent_testing::await_until!` only for side effects without a signal.
- Servers in tests bind port 0 and run through the runtime handle
  (`builder.without_signals().build()?.start().await?`).
- Database tests use `sekvent-testing` containers (one database per test);
  they are `#[ignore]`d unless `SEKVENT_DOCKER_TESTS=1`, which the gate sets.
- See the `rust-testing` skill for speed and flake work.

### Updating sekvent

- `cargo sekvent sdk update` moves the locked sekvent revision and the pinned
  third-party set together. `cargo sekvent deps check` reports drift.
- Do not bump a dependency that sekvent pins on your own; update sekvent.
